  await d.list({ title: 'The Distortion Lab: The Growth Decision', fontSize: 26, rows: [
    { icon: 'FaUsers', label: 'Groups of 4–6:', text: 'different functions represented' },
    { icon: 'FaBookOpen', label: '5 minutes:', text: 'read the scenario individually and silently' },
    { icon: 'FaUserTie', label: 'Assigned roles:', text: 'no self-selection' },
    { icon: 'FaComments', label: '10–12 minutes:', text: 'discussion without facilitator intervention' },
    { icon: 'FaHandPaper', gold: true, label: 'Stop before consensus:', text: 'has anyone identified the white space yet?' }],
    notes: N(
      'THE DISTORTION LAB: THE GROWTH DECISION (Integration Simulation · Printable)\nTime: 20–25 minutes including setup, exercise, and debrief (slides 33–36).',
      'Preparation: Print the exercise using the gold “Print Exercise” button in the facilitator file before the session begins. Each group needs one printed copy, or participants can work from the screen. Groups of 4–6 work best — assign roles across the group so that different functions are represented.',
      'Participant activity: Participants complete this activity in their own file (Section 6 · The Distortion Lab: The Growth Decision). Their file holds the objective, the scenario context, the Round 1 task, Phase 2 — Board Options and the debrief questions. The Phase 1 group data is in the facilitator file only: distribute it separately to each group.',
      'Running the exercise:\n1. Allow 5 minutes for participants to read the scenario individually and silently.\n2. Assign each participant (or pair) a functional role — do not allow self-selection. Functional attachment to an assigned role is part of the learning.\n3. Run the group discussion for 10–12 minutes without facilitator intervention. Observe where dominant voices emerge, where functions dig in, and where the white space goes unaddressed.\n4. Stop the group before they reach consensus and ask: “Has anyone identified the white space yet — the gap between all your individual positions and the actual enterprise outcome?”',
      'Objective: To demonstrate how strategic distortion forms before decisions are made, and how collective intelligence must be deliberately structured to arrive at an integrated enterprise decision.',
      'Scenario Context. Company: Apex Manufacturing · Industry: Industrial Components.\nApex Manufacturing is a mid-sized industrial components company with a strong regional reputation. The board has placed pressure on the executive team to accelerate growth while maintaining financial stability and operational integrity. The executive team must determine the most appropriate strategic direction for the next 12–36 months.',
      'Key facilitation insight: The Distortion Lab is designed to produce bias-driven discussion even in a room full of people who have just spent hours learning about bias. This is intentional. Use it to demonstrate that structural design is what protects decision quality.') });
