      'Content: From Fragmented Thinking to Collective Intelligence — leaders typically form a strategic position before options are formally presented. This demonstrates how bias shapes decision-making early in the process. Collective intelligence requires deliberate integration of partial realities.\nThe quality of strategy execution is a function of the quality of the thinking environment.',
